  "manual_obligations": [
    "All theta-PSH potentials descend uniquely; local product sections recover positivity downstairs.",
    "Ordinary order and normalization are preserved by a surjective map.",
    "The existing submersion multiplier-ideal foundation is reused; extended principal curve ideals detect equality on the base.",
    "Upper regularization commutes in product coordinates; both envelope fixed-point spaces are transported.",
    "Bounded truncations depend on one complex coordinate; decreasing local Hessians have rank at most one, so all top-degree truncation measures vanish for n>=2.",
    "Every ordinary representative, not just each model, has zero mass; the upper and lower singularity volumes both vanish.",
    "Proper submersion fiber integration is smooth and positive; dd^c gamma^(n-1)=0 makes the fiber volume harmonic, hence constant on the compact connected curve.",
    "Signed trace pullback uses Jordan decomposition; disjoint inverse-image carriers give equality of total variation, not merely an upper bound.",
    "Polar restriction commutes with submersion pullback even for nonatomic measures.",
    "The normalized trace is exactly curve polar total variation, so independence of the Gauduchon form, completeness, geodesics and diameter follow at the full-model-space scope.",
    "Analytic singularities correspond by pullback and local holomorphic sections; every analytic model is ideal.",
    "Density uses positive non-pluripolar mass on the base curve only; all its upstairs pullbacks still have zero top-degree mass.",
    "Atomic projection gives the unique nearest point and diffuse-polar-mass defect; no general higher-dimensional model realization is inferred.",
    "Pushforward of a smooth positive volume form is smooth positive on the curve, giving the explicit L1 domination.",
    "All stretching competitors descend; convex combinations preserve pole values without subtracting infinities.",
    "The arbitrary-background ideal-obstacle reprojection theorem applies to smooth obstacles upstairs, which need not descend.",
    "Critical or multiple fibers are excluded; no bounded mass property of an ambient Hermitian form is needed.",
    "All eight new/recent arXiv payloads match631 exactly; no new complete-title reading or history-gap closure is claimed.",
    "The selected six-sphere paper has singular/multiple fibers and an external starting-construction dependency; its assertions are not adopted."
  ],
